{
  "case_id": "2020-20-382",
  "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States made a strategic decision to steer the cleanup of the Ordot Dump away from CERCLA and to sue Guam -- and sue Guam under the Clean Water Act instead, no doubt to insulate itself from liability for its own role in building and using the dump."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's wrong for two independent reasons. First, Section 113(f)(3)(B) of CERCLA requires a resolution of CERCLA liability to trigger a CERCLA contribution claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Garre, under -- the position of the United States points out -- points out an incongruity in --in your position, which is that you want to imply a term like \"under CERCLA\" into Section 113, but you're bringing this -- the case under Section 107 yourself, where you don't want to imply such a term."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It resolved the claims, counsel, not the liability, but the claims, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And then can you kind of explain for a moment your argument about the preemptive effect of -- of the government's position for state contribution laws and what that would look like?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Guam",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "interpretation does here is to import this, you know, discrete CERCLA contribution claim as -- you know, into other federal statutes and to override other state laws that deal with cost contribution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Guam",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the trap for the unwary that, you know, is -- is epitomized by this case, that you would be settling a claim under a different statute to which the United States itself enjoys immunity, which is through the Clean Water Act, and that somehow that settlement would trigger a CERCLA contribution right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think that you could have a CERCLA recovery for, say, penalties under other environmental provisions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why shouldn't it matter why a person\ninitiates an activity? It -- it seems to me,\njust for the reasons Justice Alito just said,\nthe simplest reason, if \"response action\" is\nCERCLA-specific in terms of all of the\nactivities that can be, why should we build that"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Suri",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "These are provisions that show that CERCLA uses\nthe word \"response\" to refer to actions taken\nunder other statutes, including the Clean Water\nAct itself. This is on page 14, Section\n9604(k)(12)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-20-382",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bfb527815e386b669231b2a817dca41453430433818eadfcdd7888e85dd5d945",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bfb527815e38-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I understand the government's argument, (3)(B),\nreads (3)(B) as liability for response action to\ninclude settlements with states under state law,\nand then (3)(C), you read any -- all those\nsettlements now have to be governed by federal\nlaw and, just like that, pretty much every state\ncontribution regime is preempted."
    },
